          <!-- Seasonal Box -->
          <rect x="180" y="190" width="440" height="130" fill="var(--bg)" rx="8" stroke="var(--line)" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <text x="400" y="218" fill="var(--text)" font-family="Space Grotesk, sans-serif" font-size="15" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle">Annual Daylight Saving Cycle in Chicago</text>
          <text x="400" y="250" fill="var(--muted)" font-size="13" text-anchor="middle">• Second Sunday in March: Advances 1 hour to Central Daylight Time (CDT, UTC-5)</text>
          <text x="400" y="278" fill="var(--muted)" font-size="13" text-anchor="middle">• First Sunday in November: Reverts 1 hour to Central Standard Time (CST, UTC-6)</text>
          <text x="400" y="306" fill="var(--accent)" font-size="13" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle">IANA Identifier: America/Chicago</text>
        </svg>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
      <h2>Daylight Saving Time Schedule & Transition Rules for Chicago (2026–2028)</h2>
      <p>
        In accordance with the Energy Policy Act of 2005, Chicago follows standard North American Daylight Saving Time rules. Clocks jump forward by one hour on the second Sunday of March at 2:00 AM local time, and fall back by one hour on the first Sunday of November at 2:00 AM local time.
      </p>

      <div class="table-responsive">
        <table class="comparison-table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Year</th>
              <th>DST Begins (Clocks Spring Forward +1 hr)</th>
              <th>DST Ends (Clocks Fall Back -1 hr)</th>
              <th>Active Summer Offset</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>2026</strong></td>
              <td>March 8, 2026 (2:00 AM CST &rarr; 3:00 AM CDT)</td>
              <td>November 1, 2026 (2:00 AM CDT &rarr; 1:00 AM CST)</td>
              <td>CDT (UTC-5)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>2027</strong></td>
              <td>March 14, 2027 (2:00 AM CST &rarr; 3:00 AM CDT)</td>
              <td>November 7, 2027 (2:00 AM CDT &rarr; 1:00 AM CST)</td>
              <td>CDT (UTC-5)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>2028</strong></td>
              <td>March 12, 2028 (2:00 AM CST &rarr; 3:00 AM CDT)</td>
              <td>November 5, 2028 (2:00 AM CDT &rarr; 1:00 AM CST)</td>
              <td>CDT (UTC-5)</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <p>
        During the CDT period, local morning daylight arrives earlier relative to UTC, providing extended evening sunlight over Lake Michigan and downtown Chicago.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
      <h2>Chicago Financial Market Hours & Global Trading Coordination</h2>
      <p>
        Chicago is world-renowned for its financial market operations. The <strong>CME Group</strong> (encompassing the Chicago Mercantile Exchange, Chicago Board of Trade, and NYMEX) handles trillions of dollars in interest rate, equity index, agricultural commodity, and foreign exchange futures daily.
      </p>
      <p>
